Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||11:33 PM||||people in high school tend to be IMMATURE... so it's no wonder they damaged your car. I've only been in college for 4 months, and I can already see a huge difference between college students and high school students.. sure the drinking is the same... but in general, they tend to act more responsible, and respectful to one another. I never saw that in high school.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||11:43 PM||||JohnnyK, I'm sure he didn't mean anything personal by that first comment... (but I could be wrong of course..)<P>and Count, calm down, eh? As a friend, I'm just saying you gotta stop letting people get to you... if I let all the annoying idiots who bugged me actually tick me off enough to lose my temper, then there'd be a lot of VERY injured people around...... (I used to have a very short temper back in elementary school, but I calmed down throughout high school... and college is generally a pretty cool place. I don't think I've yelled at anyone since I got here..)<P>I'm not gonna say some sappy "let's all be friends" speech.. but come on guys.. chill.. at least *try* to respect each other enough to ignore them...<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-13-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000011||FieroLisa||12-13-2000||11:46 PM||||I go to a fairly small college (about 3,000 people) and I've notice it's still a lot like high school! Still the same old gossip going round and round...<BR>As for respect to cars-well I was taking 2 of my wayyy to drunk friends back to their dorms and one of them kept purposefully pouring her beer all over the parked cars she passed. And she's a senior too- so it's not like she has much high school left in her! Guess maturity depends on the person, not the age.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||11:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I go to a fairly small college (about 3,000 people) and I've notice it's still a lot like high school! Still the same old gossip going round and round...<BR>As for respect to cars-well I was taking 2 of my wayyy to drunk friends back to their dorms and one of them kept purposefully pouring her beer all over the parked cars she passed. And she's a senior too- so it's not like she has much high school left in her! Guess maturity depends on the person, not the age.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>True true.. I go to a fairly large college (11,000 full time students, 60,000 part time) but in general I've found people here to be actually pretty nice.. except the drunks. every thursday is Pub Night at the campus bar, and people tend to be very loud all thursday night... which is annoying when I have an 8:05 lecture on friday morning!<P>I don't know how much maturity comes into play when a person is totally drunk... but I'm glad I don't have to worry about acting like that myself, as I don't drink..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
