Z||000015||Hank is Here||12-14-2000||02:02 AM||||Okay, small college story.  I started at a samll campus of Penn State about 1300 people or so.  I was driving my 66 CJ5 jeep with softtop.  Needless to say- no security, heck I have to take out the rotor because I know the ignition is easy to bugger.  Well I found a recliner in the back of it once. Another time I went to use it and it was stolen.  I was walking to the cops to report it, then saw it in a small side parking lot.  Turns out some people discovered that it had no steering lock, I always needed to keep an eye on it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Oreif||12-14-2000||02:14 AM||||I had someone move around my sparkplug wires once. (69 Catalina, hood opened from outside) I also happened to get my brake lines cut! I did find the person who cut my brake lines...... Do you know what happens to a GM positraction rear end on a mid- 70's Grand Prix when someone drains the fluid out of it and the owner hits about 70 mph on a highway at night? He does now!!!!! It's really amazing at how much heat and force is generated when there is no lubrication.<P><BR>Revenge is a dish best served COLD.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
